136
00:06:51,086 --> 00:06:54,176
Oh yeah, plan Easy S tier.

137
00:06:54,256 --> 00:06:57,216
If you hit shift and tab on Cloud Code, Cloud goes into plan mode.

138
00:06:57,296 --> 00:07:04,336
Instead of reading and making changes, it reads your code more thoroughly, writes up a full plan, and it shows it to you before doing a single thing.

139
00:07:04,462 --> 00:07:06,336
And then you can either approve it or deny it.

140
00:07:06,416 --> 00:07:09,056
This feature is a must for Cloud models, I think.

141
00:07:09,230 --> 00:07:14,896
You get a higher quality result since now the model takes the time to explore and think about its actions before doing something.

142
00:07:15,056 --> 00:07:21,216
It's also way easier to catch a mistake in a plan than in like 3,000 lines of code and 12 different files it modifies.

143
00:07:21,376 --> 00:07:23,640
I recommend using plan mode for a big task.

144
00:07:23,856 --> 00:07:28,416
Don't use it for small tasks like typos, renaming variables, or small design changes.

145
00:07:28,576 --> 00:07:30,788
That's just a waste and you don't get much better results.

